  "description": "A multi-modal face processing dataset combining simultaneously recorded MEG and EEG with structural MRI from 18 participants. Participants viewed famous, unfamiliar, and scrambled faces and made a symmetry judgment by button press. The data are a curated repackaging of the MEEG portion of ds000117, with reorganized event logs, Hierarchical Event Descriptor (HED) annotations, and EEGLAB-format EEG.",
  "methods_description": "Eighteen participants took part in two sessions three months apart, one with fMRI and one with simultaneous MEG and EEG. In each, they viewed photographs of famous, unfamiliar, and scrambled faces and pressed one of two keys to give a yes/no judgment of facial symmetry. Each face was shown twice, with the repeat either immediate or delayed by 5-15 presentations. Preprocessing extracted EEG channels from the MEG/EEG fif files, added fiducials, renamed EOG/EKG channels, extracted events and button presses, removed spurious event types, corrected a 34 ms latency shift, added HED annotations, and saved the result in EEGLAB .set format.",
